From: grimtickle-overlay <overlay@grimtickle.local>
Date: Wed, 02 Jul 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Gentoo: stub Rust APT export functions — no APT on Gentoo

With the "cache" feature of proxmox-apt removed (patch 1/2), functions that
call proxmox_apt::list_available_apt_update() and proxmox_apt::update_database()
no longer compile because those symbols are gated behind the "cache" feature.

This patch replaces ALL #[export] bodies in:
  - pve-rs/src/apt/repositories.rs     (PVE::RS::APT::Repositories XS)
  - common/src/apt/repositories.rs     (Proxmox::RS::APT::Repositories XS)

with stubs that return Err("APT not available on Gentoo").

Also stubs send_updates_available() in pve-rs/src/lib.rs to return Ok(())
instead of calling proxmox_apt notification code that references APTUpdateInfo
from the now-absent cache feature context.

These functions are never called on Gentoo because:
  1. PVE::API2::APT (Perl) is independently stubbed with 501 responses
  2. No Perl code reaches these XS symbols via any other code path

The stubs exist purely so the perlmod-generated XS bindings compile cleanly.

---
 common/src/apt/repositories.rs | 58 ++++-------
 pve-rs/src/apt/repositories.rs | 34 ++-----
 pve-rs/src/lib.rs               |  8 +-
 3 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 80 deletions(-)

